---
import Base from "../layouts/base.astro";
---

<Base title="Privacy Policy — Capy Budget">
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-16">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-warm-800">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-warm-400">Last updated: March 2026</p>

    <div class="mt-8 space-y-8 text-warm-600 leading-relaxed">
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-warm-800">The short version</h2>
        <p>
          Capy Budget is a local-first application. Your financial data never leaves your
          computer unless you explicitly choose to sync it via a service like iCloud or
          Dropbox. We don't collect, store, or transmit any of your data.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-warm-800">Data storage</h2>
        <p>
          All budget data is stored as plain CSV files in a folder you choose on your
          local filesystem. The application does not use any cloud database, remote server,
          or third-party storage service.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-warm-800">No telemetry</h2>
        <p>
          The desktop application does not include any analytics, crash reporting,
          or telemetry. No usage data is collected or transmitted.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-warm-800">Intelligence layer</h2>
        <p>
          The optional AI features use Claude Code running locally on your machine.
          When you use smart import or other AI-powered features, your data is processed
          by the Claude CLI on your device. We do not have access to the content of
          these interactions. Please refer to
          <a
            href="https://www.anthropic.com/privacy"
            class="text-brand underline hover:text-brand-light"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
          >
            Anthropic's privacy policy
          </a>
          for details on how Claude processes data.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-warm-800">Web demo</h2>
        <p>
          The web demo at demo.capybudget.app runs entirely in your browser. It uses
          preset sample data and does not persist anything. No data is sent to any server.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-warm-800">This website</h2>
        <p>
          This website is hosted on Vercel. Vercel may collect standard web server logs
          (IP address, browser type, pages visited). We do not use cookies or any
          third-party tracking scripts. See
          <a
            href="https://vercel.com/legal/privacy-policy"
            class="text-brand underline hover:text-brand-light"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
          >
            Vercel's privacy policy
          </a>
          for details.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-warm-800">Open source</h2>
        <p>
          Capy Budget is open source under the MIT license. You can audit the
          entire codebase on
          <a
            href="https://github.com/vladimir-e/capybudget"
            class="text-brand underline hover:text-brand-light"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
          >
            GitHub
          </a>
          to verify these claims.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-warm-800">Contact</h2>
        <p>
          For privacy-related questions, open an issue on
          <a
            href="https://github.com/vladimir-e/capybudget/issues"
            class="text-brand underline hover:text-brand-light"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
          >
            GitHub
          </a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
